      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A complex ballistocardiographic and gammacardiographic investigation was carried out in 62 patients with coronary heart disease; ballistocardiographic and gammacardiographic indices have been compared. We established pathologic ballistocardiographic changes, which indicate a disturbance of the myocardial contractile function. Considerable changes of central haemodynamics, studied by means of gammacardiography, were recorded. There is a relationship between ballistocardiographic indices of the myocardial contractile function and radiocardiographic indices of central haemodynamics."},
